# Step one on every FAC ticket: fill in "Rules that apply"

When you are working from a GitHub Issue in ralphjohnson-cursor/factory-demo whose title starts with a FAC key (for example `FAC-1: ...`), do this BEFORE writing or changing any code.

1. Read the issue (key, summary, description, the Jurisdiction(s), and any Feature area).
2. For each jurisdiction, look in the FACCTX rule pages, which are the `rules/` folder of ralphjohnson-cursor/factory-demo-docs (`rules/AS-XX-NNN.md`, labelled by jurisdiction and feature area).
3. From each matching page, take the rule ID (AS-XX-NNN), the one-line summary, the full rule text and the page link (https://github.com/ralphjohnson-cursor/factory-demo-docs/blob/main/rules/AS-XX-NNN.md).
4. Post ONE comment on the issue in this format:

   Rules that apply (auto-filled from FACCTX)
   - AS-DE-002: <summary>
     <full rule text>
     Source: <rule page link>
   (one entry per rule)

5. If a jurisdiction has no matching page, say so in the comment and stop. Do not guess a rule.
6. After that comment is posted, write or update `.spin/rules-applied.json` before changing code. The file is what CI reads. CI does not read the issue or the docs repo. Shape:
   - `ticket`: the FAC key
   - `rules`: one entry per rule in the comment, each with `rule_id`, `jurisdiction`, and `source_url` (the rule page link from the comment)
   Copy those three fields from the comment. Do not put the rule text in the file. A malformed file fails the validator in `tests/helpers/rules-applied.ts` (schema: `.spin/rules-applied.schema.json`).
7. Only then start the change. Every rule ID in that comment and in `.spin/rules-applied.json` must be:
   - listed in the PR description, and
   - covered by at least one test whose name or comment includes the rule ID.

Never invent rules, paraphrase rule text, or pull rules from anywhere other than FACCTX. The docs repo is the source of record.
